5.

APPLICATIONS OF DIODES

Overview

This topic studies the characteristics of silicon diodes and their use for component
protection and as half-wave rectifiers for AC circuits. The use of zener diodes in
voltage regulation circuits is also covered.

Electronic Skills

This topic provides opportunities for learners to model and simulate diode circuits,
taking measurements with multimeters and oscilloscopes, and plotting results to
demonstrate the operation of the diode.

Mathematical Skills

There are a number of opportunities for the development of mathematical skills in this
topic. These include: translating information between graphical and numerical form;
plotting two variables from experimental or other data; and interpreting data
presented in graphical form.

Learners should be able to:

(a)

describe the I-V characteristics of a silicon diode

(b)

describe the use of diodes for component protection in DC circuits and half-
wave rectification of AC circuits

(c)

describe the use of zener diodes in voltage regulation circuits.

